artwork title, artist name, price, and a View Details button.- Add search, categories, featured artists, trending videos, and recently uploaded work.- Use an elegant, professional visual style with excellent mobile responsiveness.4. Video posting featureCreate a dedicated Video Posts section where authorized registered users can:- Select and upload a video from their device.- Enter a video title and description.- Upload or select a thumbnail.- Choose a category and add tags.- Preview the video before posting.- Publish, edit, and delete their own posts.- Browse videos in a responsive feed.- Play videos with standard playback controls.- Like videos, comment, and share a video link.- Open an artist's profile from a video post.- Display the creator's name, upload date, and video description.Accept common video formats such as MP4 and WebM where supported. Validate file types and file sizes, show upload progress, and display helpful error messages.Do not pretend that a video has been uploaded permanently if it is only stored temporarily in the browser. Prepare the application for persistent video storage using Supabase Storage or another suitable backend. Keep secrets and private API keys out of frontend code.5. Art and photography marketplace- Allow artists to list physical artwork, photographs, and digital downloads.- Include title, description, creator, category, price, image, and availability.- Provide artwork detail pages and a working shopping cart demo.- Support custom commission requests with a description, budget, and reference image.- Include clear distinctions between physical products and downloadable products.6. Accounts and profilesDesign registration and login screens.User profiles should support:- Profile picture and display name.- Phone number and address fields.- Artist biography and social links.- Uploaded artworks and video posts.- Order history and saved items.Use a proper authentication backend when implementing real accounts. Do not expose users' p